                <pb facs="0358" n="350" xml:id="pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4352: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-30T17:00:00-05:00">September 30, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 1—9:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>185. Your instruction number 198, September 20. Amortization Moratorium Agreement
                    signed today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For the text of Supplementary Financial Agreement between the United States
                        and Haiti, signed at Port-au-Prince, September 30, 1941, see Executive
                        Agreement Series No. 224, or 55 Stat. (pt. 2) 1385.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
